cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Competency Restoration Dashboard Data: A Reproducible Five-State Panel of Legal-Deadline Compliance for Psychiatric Competency Restoration (Washington, Oregon, Colorado, Texas, California)"
abstract: >-
  A harmonized, source-linked dataset of competency-restoration timeliness and waitlist
  measures for five U.S. states, each operating under a different legal mechanism enforcing
  (or, for Texas, newly ordering) competency-restoration admission deadlines: Washington
  (federal consent decree), Oregon (federal injunction), Colorado (federal consent decree,
  court-appointed Special Master), Texas (no binding deadline until a July 2026 ruling, under
  appeal), and California (a state-court mandate). A data-and-methods resource; it does not
  report study findings. Updated periodically as new source reports are published.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Rai
    given-names: Sudhanshu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2447-0336"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - competency to stand trial
  - incompetent to stand trial
  - competency restoration
  - Trueblood
  - Mink Bowman
  - Center for Legal Advocacy v. Barnes
  - Stiavetti v. Clendenin
  - court monitoring
  - forensic mental health
  - open data
  - reproducibility
url: "https://competencyrestoration.org"
